{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>עֲבֹדַת מַתָּנָה אֶתֵּן אֶת כְּהֻנַּתְכֶם</b> – \"It shall be to you as a gift,\" the language of Rashi. Meaning that it is to you an absolute gift, so that the stranger who offers shall be liable to death. But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that it says, \"And you shall perform the service of the priesthood,\" and it is not for you a service of servitude like the labor of the servants of kings, but rather a service of a great gift I have given you in it, for honor and splendor from Me, as the Sages expounded (Sotah 15a): \"לְמָשְׁחָה\" (for anointing) — for greatness, in the manner that kings eat."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:34.107149707Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}